---
import PageContainer from "../components/layout/PageContainer.astro";
import ContentSection from "../components/ui/ContentSection.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  heading="A brief autobiography"
  description="How mathematics, computer science, research, and systems work fit together for me."
>
  <PageContainer class="space-y-6">
    <ContentSection id="background" title="Background">
      <p>
        I’m a Computer Science and Mathematics Joint Honours Co-op student at
        the University of Manitoba, with a minor in Statistics. I was born and
        raised in Winnipeg, and my choice of degree has always been driven by
        curiosity: I enjoy the rigour of mathematics and the process of turning
        an idea into a working program.
      </p>
      <p>
        My interest in computing began with programming in high school and grew
        into a broader curiosity about how computers work—from the logic of
        algorithms to the design of operating systems.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="interests" title="Technical interests">
      <p>
        My main academic interests include discrete algorithms, computational
        geometry, point-set topology, and number theory. On the systems side,
        I’m interested in low-level, operating-system, and embedded programming.
      </p>
      <p>
        I enjoy moving between theory and implementation: analyzing an algorithm
        on paper, proving why it works, and then building a clear, efficient
        implementation. I have worked with Java, Python, C, C++, JavaScript,
        LaTeX, Linux, and tools such as Neovim.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="research-and-teaching" title="Research and teaching">
      <p>
        In Summer 2025, I researched a problem in computational geometry and
        discrete optimization with Dr. Stéphane Durocher at the University of
        Manitoba. I also enjoy teaching mathematics and theoretical computer
        science, whether in tutorials, the Math Help Centre, or an informal
        conversation about an interesting problem.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="outside-work" title="Outside the work">
      <p>
        Away from coursework and projects, I like reading, learning new tools,
        refining my Linux development setup, and spending time with friends.
        This site is where I collect the work I’m proud of and document what I
        learn next.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>
  </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>
